{
  "id": "COMPOUND:17827 - PROTEIN:5940",
  "verbalization": "Ethyl 3-(methylthio)propionate appears to have a potential relationship with Carboxylesterase 2 through a series of target-mediated pathways. The evidence suggests that this compound targets Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Diplotrin A, 5-Hydroxy-2-Methylchromone-7-O-Rutinoside, and Flavipin. All of these compounds are implicated in the inhibition of Carboxylesterase 2, a key enzyme involved in the metabolism of various substrates. The shared targeting of Thioredoxin, mitochondrial across these pathways indicates a possible common mechanism of action, possibly involving the modulation of redox processes or the disruption of mitochondrial function. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Ethyl 3-(methylthio)propionate and Carboxylesterase 2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
